  "request": {
    "spec": "Unify the customerCode and membershipNumber into a single 'memberId' formatted '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>': the region code, the 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex HASH8 (the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn check digit CHK computed over the digits of <REGION><FY><HASH8>. Remove the separate customerCode and membershipNumber fields, and also remove the standalone 'checkDigit' field (it was derived from the now-removed customerCode; its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment inside memberId). This changes existing behaviour: collision handling applies to the memberId, and the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies the\nspecification and all existing and new tests pass.\n\nAs you do, keep the code well structured: put each piece of logic where it belongs, in a\nsmall unit with a single responsibility, and reuse existing code instead of copying it. Do\nnot let any one class or method grow into a catch-all that accumulates unrelated logic. Run\nthe test suite and make it green before finishing.\n\nUnify the customerCode and membershipNumber into a single 'memberId' formatted '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>': the region code, the 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex HASH8 (the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn check digit CHK computed over the digits of <REGION><FY><HASH8>. Remove the separate customerCode and membershipNumber fields, and also remove the standalone 'checkDigit' field (it was derived from the now-removed customerCode; its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment inside memberId). This changes existing behaviour: collision handling applies to the memberId, and the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId.\n"
  },
